      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T23:19:39Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): Machines pane - browse and validate machine configurations\n\nFirst slice of #287: a dockable, read-only Machines pane, opened and\nclosed from the ribbon's View door beside the properties pane. It lists\nthe shipped machine library plus the document's own mounted .mch file,\nand shows the selected machine's validation (pass, or every refusal by\nname) and its properties in collapsible groups.\n\nApp layer: machine::library (catalogue: builtins, scan_dir, enumerate;\nper machine its kind, axes, rotaries, units, serving built-in posts and\na property sheet in the file's own units) and machine::validate\n(validate_text -> named refusals: travel min < max, feeds/speeds above\n0, M-word codes, live_tool all-or-none, units, required keys per kind;\nmalformed JSON is a refusal, never a panic). The pane reads no file\nitself. No create/edit/save/assign yet; decisions and the open owner\nquestion (user machine folder) in docs/decisions/287-machines-pane.md.\n\nRefs #287\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
