  {
    "sha": "cb293f30cefab0ba18b5fbd1cf02717a41e2e450",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVmlK7doAKGNiMjkzZjMwY2VmYWIwYmExOGI1ZmJkMWNmMDI3MTdhNDFlMmU0NTA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T02:54:36Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T02:54:36Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): Machines pane \"Use for this setup\" assigns the selected machine\n\nThe Machines pane's detail view gains a \"Use for this setup\" button. It\nqueues CommandKind::UseCatalogueMachine, which the state drain turns\ninto the existing LoadMachine command via the new\nLoadMachine::from_catalogue - the same carrier the Setup pane's machine\npicker, editor Apply and ribbon machine door use, since the machine is\nthe document singleton (there is no per-setup machine). Undo restores\nthe previous machine; redo assigns it again.\n\nfrom_catalogue re-reads the built-in text or the file and re-validates\nit, refusing by the first refusal, so a refused file never mounts even\nif queued directly. The pane disables the button with the reason shown\n(and as hover text) via MachineEntry::assign_block: a validation\nrefusal, or the machine already being the setup's.\n\nDecision (docs/decisions/384-machines-use-for-setup.md): the Setup\npane's machine editor window folds into the Machines pane as its edit\nmode when the edit slice lands; unchanged here.\n\nPinned by machine_assign (app) and the machines_pane ui tests.\n\nFixes #384\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "372e4d04fe32706f0c54fd11acdab0bbddceb070",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/372e4d04fe32706f0c54fd11acdab0bbddceb070"
