  {
    "sha": "35cfa074960b5176503e0ea5d3fd916ffae2fde4",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVmlK7doAKDM1Y2ZhMDc0OTYwYjUxNzY1MDNlMGVhNWQzZmQ5MTZmZmFlMmZkZTQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T02:59:09Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T02:59:09Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): \"Use for this setup\" follows the per-setup machine route\n\nMain gained per-setup machines (#343): a machine verb lands on the\nactive setup's own machine (SetSetupMachine) when it owns one, else on\nthe document's (LoadMachine). The Machines pane's \"Use for this setup\"\nnow takes that same route (State::mount_catalogue via route_machine),\nso an active setup with its own machine gets the selected machine and\nthe document's machine is left alone.\n\nThe read-and-validate step moves to machine::library::read_for_assign,\nshared by the ui route and by LoadMachine::from_catalogue and the new\nSetSetupMachine::from_catalogue: a refused file never mounts. The\n\"already this setup's machine\" check reads machine::of, the active\nsetup's effective machine on main.\n\nPinned by machine_assign::a_setup_with_its_own_machine_takes_the_catalogue_machine\nand machines_pane::use_for_this_setup_replaces_an_own_machine_and_leaves_the_document_alone.\nThe decisions file drops the earlier \"no per-setup machine\" premise.\n\nFixes #384\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
